- Cost per solved task: $0.17 on Internal Bench Hard versus $3.40 for Opus 5. [Agent benchmarks](https://browser-use.com/benchmarks/agents)

**4. The lowest listed browser-hour price in our comparison, and you only pay for what you use.** Browser Use Cloud has no subscriptions, no plans, and no commitment: buy credits when you need them, they never expire, and browsers are metered by the minute at $0.02 per browser-hour with residential proxies at $5/GB. Browserbase and Hyperbrowser need a monthly plan past their free tier and list $0.10 to $0.12 per browser-hour; Steel is $0.10 pay as you go, or $0.08 on its $250/month plan: four to six times $0.02. Of the seven providers in our [cloud browser comparison](https://browser-use.com/cloud-browsers.md), Browser Use Cloud has the lowest listed browser time at 100, 300 and 1,000 parallel browsers, and concurrency rises with lifetime spend instead of with a plan tier. We love simplicity and reliability without commitment, from solo devs to enterprises.

