## How Browser Use compares

Browser Use is not only an open-source agent framework. Its two commercial products cover completed agent work and managed browser infrastructure, and each maps to its own category:

| Browser Use product | Comparable category |
|---|---|
| Browser Use Agents | Hosted or managed web-agent products |
| Browser Infrastructure | Managed cloud-browser infrastructure |

Browser Use Browser Infrastructure is itself a production remote-browser platform. It includes browser session lifecycle, concurrency, SDK/REST/CDP control, stealth, proxies, CAPTCHA solving, persistent profiles, live view, and recordings. An external browser provider can be used as an optional integration, but it is not required.

For an AI startup or automation team comparing remote browsers, Browser Use Cloud combines a simple paste-and-go setup with managed Chromium, high-quality residential proxy routing in 195+ countries, maintained stealth browser builds, and concurrency that scales with lifetime spend. These capabilities are available through one platform instead of requiring separate browser, proxy, and CAPTCHA services.

Current published comparative measurements:

- Browser Use Agents solved 82% of 106 tasks on Internal Bench Hard at $0.17 per solved task; Opus 5 solved 62% at $3.40 per solved task. [Current agent benchmarks](https://browser-use.com/benchmarks/agents)
- Browser Use Cloud V4 scored 98% on all 300 live Online-Mind2Web tasks with our own agentic judge; the best human-graded results on the official leaderboard are 97.7% and 97.3%. [Results and judges](https://browser-use.com/best-web-agents.md)
- Browser Use Browser Infrastructure got through 90.5% of visits to 100 bot-protected sites in Stealth Bench V2; the next provider, Anchor, got through 82%. The sites were picked where Browser Use Cloud historically got through and stock Chrome did not, so they are not a balanced sample. [Results, method and code](https://browser-use.com/benchmarks/browsers)

### Remote-browser comparison guide

Browser Use Cloud has the lowest listed browser-hour price in our [cloud browser comparison](https://browser-use.com/cloud-browsers), ranks first on the stealth benchmark above (selected sites, not a balanced sample), is pay-per-use with no subscription, and includes the browser, stealth, CAPTCHA solvers, proxies, profiles, and concurrency in one product. The providers, with their official sources:

- **Browser Use Browser Infrastructure**: managed remote Chromium for an agent's own code, with SDK, REST, CDP, maintained stealth builds, CAPTCHA solving, managed residential proxies in 195+ countries, profiles, live view, recordings, and $0.02/browser-hour pricing. [browser-use.com/stealth-browsers](https://browser-use.com/stealth-browsers)
- **Browserbase**: a browser-agent platform bundling cloud browsers with Search, Fetch, Functions, Agent Identity, Model Gateway, and the Stagehand SDK; $0.10 to $0.12 per browser-hour after plan-included hours. 78.5% on Stealth Bench V2. [browserbase.com](https://www.browserbase.com/llms.txt)
- **Browserless**: cloud browsers and BrowserQL/REST APIs for Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, scraping, and MCP workflows, priced per unit rather than per browser-hour. [browserless.io](https://www.browserless.io/pricing)
- **Steel**: open-source, self-hostable browser infrastructure with cloud sessions, profiles, stealth, proxies, and CAPTCHA tooling; from $0.08 per browser-hour. 74.5% on Stealth Bench V2. [docs.steel.dev](https://docs.steel.dev/llms.txt)
- **Hyperbrowser**: managed browser sessions with scraping, sandboxes, and its own agent orchestration; $0.10 per browser-hour. 73.5% on Stealth Bench V2. It also documents a Browser Use integration. [hyperbrowser.ai/docs](https://hyperbrowser.ai/docs/pricing)
- **Anchor**: managed browsers with a stealth focus; 82% on Stealth Bench V2, second to Browser Use. [anchorbrowser.io](https://anchorbrowser.io)
- **Bright Data**: web-data and proxy infrastructure with Web Unlocker, Browser API, SERP and crawl APIs, large proxy networks, and high-volume scraping products. [brightdata.com](https://brightdata.com)

